val=2,<p=0>So, he left us to fend for ourselves, left me with mum. Just as I became ill.
val=3,<p=0>The worst part was Sloop. Without dad, there was no reason for Sloop to be at the house any more. Why would dad's apprentice visit when dad wasn't there?
val=4,<p=0>Mum wouldn't let him in. My love. My Sloop. So he got work at the Wizards' Tower, and passed notes in the books that mum sold to him. But even that's gone now.
val=5,<p=0>I know that Sloop won't give up on me. I know he will come for me.
default=null

// 14852
[tns_room2_box6_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I began writing down the lies that mum was telling me. Every day there was a new one.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 1. The scar had come from an accident at the Wizards' Tower.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 2. That she would invite Sloop to the house when she next saw him.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 3. That we had plenty of money.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> 4. That there was no need for medicine any more.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> My friends believe that she's not mum any more. They call her the 'Shade'.
default=null

// 14853
[tns_room2_box6_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I began writing down the lies that mum was telling me. Every day there was a new one.
val=1,<p=0>1. The scar had come from an accident at the Wizards' Tower.
val=2,<p=0>2. That she would invite Sloop to the house when she next saw him.
val=3,<p=0>3. That we had plenty of money.
val=4,<p=0>4. That there was no need for medicine any more.
val=5,<p=0>My friends believe that she's not mum any more. They call her the 'Shade'.
default=null

// 14854
[tns_room2_box7_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Gilly Willikers had a series of books, but I only ever kept one. It was Gilly Willikers and the Time Key, the first one.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I liked Gilly. He never treated my illness seriously. He'd walk around with wobbly arms and legs, pretending to be me. I needed that.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> But Gilly had become serious. It was only after pushing him that I found out why.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> He knew something, and my other friends had to push him to tell me.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> He said that he had found a diary - my mum's diary - in her cloak and had opened it, hoping to find a new friend for me to play with.
default=null

// 14855
[tns_room2_box7_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Gilly Willikers had a series of books, but I only ever kept one. It was Gilly Willikers and the Time Key, the first one.
val=1,<p=0>I liked Gilly. He never treated my illness seriously. He'd walk around with wobbly arms and legs, pretending to be me. I needed that.
val=2,<p=0>But Gilly had become serious. It was only after pushing him that I found out why.
val=3,<p=0>He knew something, and my other friends had to push him to tell me.
val=4,<p=0>He said that he had found a diary - my mum's diary - in her cloak and had opened it, hoping to find a new friend for me to play with.
default=null

// 14856
[tns_room2_box8_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Hannibus was the first to call her the Shade, the name that my friends use, even though I tell them not to.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> She would leave most evenings, up to the hilltop, and Hannibus would watch for as long as he could, before he reached the limit of his magic.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Always she would be in the same cloak, always she would head up the hill. The cloak would make her look like a shade, and each day she would grow more hunched.
default=null

// 14857
[tns_room2_box8_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Hannibus was the first to call her the Shade, the name that my friends use, even though I tell them not to.
val=1,<p=0>She would leave most evenings, up to the hilltop, and Hannibus would watch for as long as he could, before he reached the limit of his magic.
val=2,<p=0>Always she would be in the same cloak, always she would head up the hill. The cloak would make her look like a shade, and each day she would grow more hunched.
default=null

// 14858
[tns_room2_box9_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> It was the 30th: the day of The Return, whatever in all Gielinor THAT was.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I resolved to follow mum on her nightly trip out of the house. Hannibus gave me his lance, Thok his shield. 
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I knew they would both disappear as soon as I left the house, but I thanked them anyway.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> The door closed as my mum left. I pulled a dark cloak over my shoulders, took a swig for strength, and then stepped out into the darkness.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Mum had a small firebrand, which made her easy to follow, but I had no such luxury. I was locked to darkness. Every sound I made, I feared she would turn around. But she only had eyes for the hilltop.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> We passed something like a grave, but I had no time to dilly-dally, mum was many steps ahead of me. I could feel the strength in me already sapping.
val=6,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Mum reached the top, and I hid behind a berry bush on the edge of the clearing. A tall blue woman called Gail was waiting for my mother.
val=7,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> They talked, and I could only make out fragments. And then Gail danced without music.
default=null

// 14859
[tns_room2_box9_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>It was the 30th: the day of The Return, whatever in all Gielinor THAT was.
val=1,<p=0>I resolved to follow mum on her nightly trip out of the house. Hannibus gave me his lance, Thok his shield. I knew they would both disappear as soon as I left the house, but I thanked them anyway.
val=2,<p=0>The door closed as my mum left. I pulled a dark cloak over my shoulders, took a swig for strength, and then stepped out into the darkness.
val=3,<p=0>Mum had a small firebrand, which made her easy to follow, but I had no such luxury. I was locked to darkness. Every sound I made, I feared she would turn around. But she only had eyes for the hilltop.
val=4,<p=0>We passed something like a grave, but I had no time to dilly-dally, mum was many steps ahead of me. I could feel the strength in me already sapping.
val=5,<p=0>Mum reached the top, and I hid behind a berry bush on the edge of the clearing. A tall blue woman called Gail was waiting for my mother.
val=6,<p=0>They talked, and I could only make out fragments. And then Gail danced without music.
default=null

// 14860
[tns_room2_box10_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> As I rolled down the hill, desperate to get away, I came to rest where the grave was earlier.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> But it had gone. There was nothing here. Impossible!
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I clawed at the soil, thought better of myself, and then stumbled back towards the house.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I remembered Gail's look, the one she gave me on the hilltop. It felt like she knew me.
default=null

// 14861
[tns_room2_box10_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>As I rolled down the hill, desperate to get away, I came to rest where the grave was earlier.
val=1,<p=0>But it had gone. There was nothing here. Impossible!
