// 14862
[tns_room2_box11_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> She was mesmerising. Gail glowed as she danced, and a thread span from her, flicking high into the air before resting in place, as if she was drawing the constellations.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Then thread upon thread layered onto each other, until a woven dome formed over the top of them - and me.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> As she danced around, I thought she caught my eye. I hid my own eyes and skulked further behind the berry bush. But she danced on.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Lights flashed, centring on the needle, and then... all was calm. Mum walked towards Gail, who looked exhausted, and laid a hand on her head.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Gail said something to my mum - something about 'doubt', about me doubting her, perhaps. Gail flashed me a look.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Whatever happened was coming to an end, and there was no time to linger. I shuffled away from the hilltop and caught a foot on a root, stumbling down to where the grave was before.
default=null

// 14863
[tns_room2_box11_text_npc]
