// 14870
[tns_room2_box15_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Baba came hopping into my room. Always made me laugh - she doesn't walk, more bounces.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> But I could see from her expression that something wasn't right. She lost her footing and tumbled into my sideboard, knocking over a medicine bottle.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> She told me that Gilly had found something, and that I should come right away.
default=null

// 14871
[tns_room2_box15_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=2>Baba came hopping into my room. Always made me laugh - she doesn't walk, more bounces.
val=1,<p=2>But I could see from her expression that something wasn't right. She lost her footing and tumbled into my sideboard, knocking over a medicine bottle.
val=2,<p=2>She told me that Gilly had found something, and that I should come right away.
default=null

// 14872
[tns_room2_box16_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Thok was one of my favourites. He knew it, of course, and would wander round the house beating his chest, calling himself 'Primrose's Champion'.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> He was going to protect me from everything, and everything was a potential threat. A twitch in a curtain was a ghost, a slammed door was a demon.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I tried to tell him that demons had better things to do than playing with doors, but he'd look at me slyly and say 'that's what they want us to think'.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I was so much happier having him around. And not just because of the threat of door demons.
default=null

// 14873
[tns_room2_box16_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=1>Thok was one of my favourites. He knew it, of course, and would wander round the house beating his chest, calling himself 'Primrose's Champion'.
val=1,<p=1>He was going to protect me from everything, and everything was a potential threat. A twitch in a curtain was a ghost, a slammed door was a demon.
val=2,<p=1>I tried to tell him that demons had better things to do than playing with doors, but he'd look at me slyly and say 'that's what they want us to think'.
val=3,<p=1>I was so much happier having him around. And not just because of the threat of door demons.
default=null

// 14874
[tns_room2_box17_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I took a dose of strength potion and, completely inelegantly, made my way to mum's bedside table, just as Gilly had told me.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I couldn't quite understand what I was reading. On each day of the diary, there were multiple entries, written in tiny text and boxed off from each other.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> I looked for yesterday's date. Again, there were multiple entries for one day.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> One was familiar: it talked about the pie she had made, and noted that she thought I looked healthier having eaten it.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> But I didn't recognise the other entries for yesterday; they were events I didn't recognise. An argument we never had. A visit to the Wizards' Tower. A burning of the pie.
val=5,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> Then I looked at tomorrow's entry: the 30th. The book was completely blank after that date.
val=6,<col=ff0000>Primrose:</col> And every entry on the 30th, of which there were many, was the same. The Return. The Return. The Return. The Return. The Return.
default=null

// 14875
[tns_room2_box17_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I took a dose of strength potion and, completely inelegantly, made my way to mum's bedside table, just as Gilly had told me.
val=1,<p=0>I couldn't quite understand what I was reading. On each day of the diary, there were multiple entries, written in tiny text and boxed off from each other.
val=2,<p=0>I looked for yesterday's date. Again, there were multiple entries for one day.
val=3,<p=0>One was familiar: it talked about the pie she had made, and noted that she thought I looked healthier having eaten it.
val=4,<p=0>But I didn't recognise the other entries for yesterday; they were events I didn't recognise. An argument we never had. A visit to the Wizards' Tower. A burning of the pie.
val=5,<p=0>Then I looked at tomorrow's entry: the 30th. The book was completely blank after that date.
val=6,<p=0>And every entry on the 30th, of which there were many, was the same. The Return. The Return. The Return. The Return. The Return.
default=null

// 14876
[tns_room2_box18_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Primrose: </col>She was so beautiful. It was breathtaking. 
val=1,<col=ff0000>Primrose: </col>I mean, she was scary too. She was about twice as big as me, even without me being hunched, and had a hundred times the strength and a million times the magic.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Primrose: </col>I desperately wanted to meet her and get to know her. I felt it in my belly, right next to my sickness.
default=null

// 14877
[tns_room2_box18_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
