// 14922
[tns_room3_box1_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It was time to say no. Perhaps it was time long ago.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> And I knew what it would mean for me, the cost for me. 
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But this wouldn't be our ending, not for any of us. I knew that the moment I saw Primrose behind the buckthorn bush.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It all clicked together. I knew what we all were in that moment. We were family.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I was going to help my family by saying no.
default=null

// 14923
[tns_room3_box1_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>It was time to say no. Perhaps it was time long ago.
val=1,<p=0>And I knew what it would mean for me, the cost for me. 
val=2,<p=0>But this wouldn't be our ending, not for any of us. I knew that the moment I saw Primrose behind the buckthorn bush.
val=3,<p=0>It all clicked together. I knew what we all were in that moment. We were family.
val=4,<p=0>I was going to help my family by saying no.
default=null

// 14924
[tns_room3_box2_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Primrose was there again, behind the buckthorn bush, as Megan begged for another Return.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Primrose had been there, without fail for the past three Returns.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Every time, The Needle took all three of us back, and every time Primrose rushed to be in bed before her mother arrived.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Megan never saw her, never thought that Primrose might have been following her. All Megan saw was a cruel fate - a daughter getting progressively ill within a time loop.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But Primrose was on the verge of dying. It was time to say no to Megan and begin what must be begun.
default=null

// 14925
[tns_room3_box2_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Primrose was there again, behind the buckthorn bush, as Megan begged for another Return. 
val=1,<p=0>Primrose had been there, without fail for the past three Returns. Every time, The Needle took all three of us back, and every time Primrose rushed to be in bed before her mother arrived.
val=2,<p=0>Megan never saw her, never thought that Primrose might have been following her. All Megan saw was a cruel fate - a daughter getting progressively ill within a time loop.
val=3,<p=0>But Primrose was on the verge of dying. It was time to say no to Megan and begin what must be begun.
default=null

// 14926
[tns_room3_box3_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Ever since Megan burned the books, something had moved in her. It was like Megan shifted aside, to be seen only occasionally.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> There was something in there with her. At first I thought she'd just abandoned her sense of self: given everything up for Primrose.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But no. There was someone in there with her. A thing.
default=null

// 14927
[tns_room3_box3_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Ever since Megan burned the books, something had moved in her. It was like Megan shifted aside, to be seen only occasionally.
val=1,<p=0>There was something in there with her. At first I thought she'd just abandoned her sense of self: given everything up for Primrose.
val=2,<p=0>But no. There was someone in there with her. A thing.
default=null

// 14928
[tns_room3_box4_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> There wasn't much left of Primrose any more. She found strength to make it up to the hilltop - she found it from somewhere - but she was rarely awake otherwise.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Often, I would let myself into the house as both Megan and Primrose were asleep. Buckthorn berry makes a rudimentary salve, and I would apply it to Primrose as she dreamed. 
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It eased her pain, but there was no stopping her fate.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I couldn't stay for long in the house, not only because I might get caught, but because I felt I was being watched. Someone, some Thing...staring at me.
default=null

// 14929
[tns_room3_box4_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>There wasn't much left of Primrose any more. She found strength to make it up to the hilltop - she found it from somewhere - but she was rarely awake otherwise.
val=1,<p=0>Often, I would let myself into the house as both Megan and Primrose were asleep. Buckthorn berry makes a rudimentary salve, and I would apply it to Primrose as she dreamed. 
val=2,<p=0>It eased her pain, but there was no stopping her fate.
val=3,<p=0>I couldn't stay for long in the house, not only because I might get caught, but because I felt I was being watched. Someone, some Thing...staring at me.
default=null

// 14930
[tns_room3_box5_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I never told Megan how much a Returning hurt. It didn't just sap the energy of the Needle - it sapped from me, too.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I would sleep, propped up next to The Needle. It would give off a little heat as it recharged, and it felt like it was doing the same to me.
default=null

// 14931
[tns_room3_box5_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I never told Megan how much a Returning hurt. It didn't just sap the energy of the Needle - it sapped from me, too.
val=1,<p=0>I would sleep, propped up next to The Needle. It would give off a little heat as it recharged, and it felt like it was doing the same to me.
default=null

// 14932
[tns_room3_box6_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Something was always going to give. We couldn't loop forever, and at some point... we would reach an ending.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> And now we've reached it. But is it a closed loop, or the start of another story?
default=null

// 14933
[tns_room3_box6_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Something was always going to give. We couldn't loop forever, and at some point... we would reach an ending.
val=1,<p=0>And now we've reached it. But is it a closed loop, or the start of another story?
default=null

// 14934
[tns_room3_box7_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I was born as I am now. I didn't have a mother, father or childhood. I was me, nothing more, and I came to... next to the Needle.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I knew what The Needle was, but I knew next to nothing about myself. It's a back-to-front way of learning about the world.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I knew how to use The Needle, what its limits were, how it used time. But I had no idea about people, the world, nothing.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I'm learning fast and leaving a trail of mistakes behind me, I am sure of it.
default=null

// 14935
[tns_room3_box7_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I was born as I am now. I didn't have a mother, father or childhood. I was me, nothing more, and I came to... next to the Needle.
val=1,<p=0>I knew what The Needle was, but I knew next to nothing about myself. It's a back-to-front way of learning about the world.
val=2,<p=0>I knew how to use The Needle, what its limits were, how it used time. But I had no idea about people, the world, nothing.
val=3,<p=0>I'm learning fast and leaving a trail of mistakes behind me, I am sure of it.
default=null

// 14936
[tns_room3_box8_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I struggled with what 'family' meant. Never having parents or siblings will do that to you.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But I've found myself pulled into Primrose and Megan's lives more and more, like a black hole.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I've tried to move on and away, but they've needed me. I've felt responsible. I've wanted to see them happy. And - if I'm honest -  I've felt happy that they needed me.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I can only imagine that is what 'family' means.
default=null

// 14937
[tns_room3_box8_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I struggled with what 'family' meant. Never having parents or siblings will do that to you.
val=1,<p=0>But I've found myself pulled into Primrose and Megan's lives more and more, like a black hole.
val=2,<p=0>I've tried to move on and away, but they've needed me. I've felt responsible. I've wanted to see them happy. And - if I'm honest -  I've felt happy that they needed me.
val=3,<p=0>I can only imagine that is what 'family' means.
default=null

// 14938
[tns_room3_box9_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> The buckthorn is a versatile bush. Its berries can be crushed and heated to make a salve, while its leaves can be used like a smelling salt, waking up the unconscious. 
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> And it makes for a great hiding spot, of course! Primrose proved that every Returning, keeping well away from Megan. 
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Is it ironic that Primrose fainted on it? I'm not sure I have a handle on irony yet.
default=null

// 14939
[tns_room3_box9_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>The buckthorn is a versatile bush. Its berries can be crushed and heated to make a salve, while its leaves can be used like a smelling salt, waking up the unconscious. 
val=1,<p=0>And it makes for a great hiding spot, of course! Primrose proved that every Returning, keeping well away from Megan. 
val=2,<p=0>Is it ironic that Primrose fainted on it? I'm not sure I have a handle on irony yet.
default=null

// 14940
[tns_room3_box10_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It was at the end of one of the Returnings, once Primrose had rushed home and Megan followed a little time after.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Primrose had hooked a small sheet of paper onto a buckthorn - a message for me.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It spoke of a necessary evil.
default=null

// 14941
[tns_room3_box10_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>It was at the end of one of the Returnings, once Primrose had rushed home and Megan followed a little time after.
val=1,<p=0>Primrose had hooked a small sheet of paper onto a buckthorn - a message for me.
val=2,<p=0>It spoke of a necessary evil.
default=null

// 14942
[tns_room3_box11_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Megan never understood why Primrose was getting progressively ill after each Returning. She would wind back in time, and everything would revert apart from the illness.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> At first she despaired, but that progressed to anger. It was a cruel fate that denied Primrose her health. Even time was fighting against her.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Just one more Returning, she would say. One more would make it right.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But Primrose was following Megan every time. Primrose was committed to ending her mother's pain.
default=null

// 14943
[tns_room3_box11_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Megan never understood why Primrose was getting progressively ill after each Returning. She would wind back in time, and everything would revert apart from the illness.
val=1,<p=0>At first she despaired, but that progressed to anger. It was a cruel fate that denied Primrose her health. Even time was fighting against her.
val=2,<p=0>Just one more Returning, she would say. One more would make it right.
val=3,<p=0>But Primrose was following Megan every time. Primrose was committed to ending her mother's pain.
default=null

// 14944
[tns_room3_box12_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Primrose fainted loudly, crashing into the buckthorn. Megan turned and I couldn't stop her from running to her.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Megan assumed the worst. She was panicking, shaking Primrose. She couldn't sense life as I could, and there was a thread of it still in Primrose.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Megan was convinced that Primrose was dead, and I couldn't convince her otherwise.
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It is cruel to think it, but I believe that Megan wanted it to be true in some way. Deep down, she wanted to end this loop she had created for herself.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> That was when I saw the knife in her hand.
default=null

// 14945
[tns_room3_box12_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>Primrose fainted loudly, crashing into the buckthorn. Megan turned and I couldn't stop her from running to her.
val=1,<p=0>Megan assumed the worst. She was panicking, shaking Primrose. She couldn't sense life as I could, and there was a thread of it still in Primrose.
val=2,<p=0>Megan was convinced that Primrose was dead, and I couldn't convince her otherwise.
val=3,<p=0>It is cruel to think it, but I believe that Megan wanted it to be true in some way. Deep down, she wanted to end this loop she had created for herself.
val=4,<p=0>That was when I saw the knife in her hand.
default=null

// 14946
[tns_room3_box13_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I'd always meant to ask Primrose if there was something in the books, something that might have been unleashed when Megan burned them.
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> But Primrose and I were kept apart by Megan. We never had the chance to talk like we did...before.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Was this Thing in Megan from the books? Ah, why did I never ask her?
default=null

// 14947
[tns_room3_box13_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>I'd always meant to ask Primrose if there was something in the books, something that might have been unleashed when Megan burned them.
val=1,<p=0>But Primrose and I were kept apart by Megan. We never had the chance to talk like we did...before.
val=2,<p=0>Was this Thing in Megan from the books? Ah, why did I never ask her?
default=null

// 14948
[tns_room3_box14_text]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> The knife slipped between my ribs. I don't remember much of what Megan said as she stood above me, but it was clear she blamed me for Primrose's death..
val=1,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Then she ran downhill, and I moved as close to the Needle as I could. My life was ebbing, but I was still able to touch the Needle.
val=2,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> I prepared to use the pausing phrase: 'Wenla'
val=3,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> Perhaps, somehow, we will be found. With the Needle, they will understand our story and save us all. Megan, Primrose and myself.
val=4,<col=ff0000>Gail:</col> It's the only way this can all be unwritten.
default=null

// 14949
[tns_room3_box14_text_npc]
inputtype=int
outputtype=string
val=0,<p=0>The knife slipped between my ribs. I don't remember much of what Megan said as she stood above me, but it was clear she blamed me for Primrose's death..
val=1,<p=0>Then she ran downhill, and I moved as close to the Needle as I could. My life was ebbing, but I was still able to touch the Needle.
val=2,<p=0>I prepared to use the pausing phrase: 'Wenla'
val=3,<p=0>Perhaps, somehow, we will be found. With the Needle, they will understand our story and save us all. Megan, Primrose and myself.
val=4,<p=0>It's the only way this can all be unwritten.
default=null

